1
00:00:01,447 --> 00:00:04,740
(peaceful guitar music)

2
00:00:08,489 --> 00:00:09,615
[Boy] What?

3
00:00:09,698 --> 00:00:11,257
The Super Scary Movie
series went up to Five?

4
00:00:11,281 --> 00:00:13,574
Seven in fact!

5
00:00:13,657 --> 00:00:14,699
For real?

6
00:00:14,782 --> 00:00:17,407
Whoa! Then the seventh
one must be really out there!

7
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:18,574
Yeah!

8
00:00:18,657 --> 00:00:21,033
It turned into a completely
different thing by Seven.

9
00:00:21,116 --> 00:00:22,950
It's not just a parody anymore.

10
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:25,134
What kind of movie is it then?

11
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:27,575
[Junpei] Hmm...

12
00:00:27,658 --> 00:00:29,260
Like a convoluted sitcom,
plus lineage horror, maybe?

13
00:00:29,284 --> 00:00:31,201
[Friend] Huh? What do you means?

14
00:00:31,284 --> 00:00:33,534
[Junpei] By a total fluke,

15
00:00:33,618 --> 00:00:35,409
the grandchild of the
main character from One

16
00:00:35,492 --> 00:00:37,034
ends up living in a shared house

17
00:00:37,118 --> 00:00:39,035
with the grandchild
of the culprit from Two

18
00:00:39,118 --> 00:00:41,911
and the grandchild of the
first person who died in Three.

19
00:00:41,993 --> 00:00:43,785
But it turns out it's
a haunted house,

20
00:00:43,869 --> 00:00:45,452
so they call in a spirit medium.

21
00:00:45,536 --> 00:00:46,077
That's pretty much the plot.

22
00:00:46,161 --> 00:00:49,244
Okay. Sounds like a bore.

23
00:00:49,328 --> 00:00:51,077
[Junpei] It bored me to death!

24
00:00:51,161 --> 00:00:53,077
So who would watch that?

25
00:00:53,161 --> 00:00:54,329
There was one cool thing.

26
00:00:54,412 --> 00:00:56,245
The guy from
five and six was in-

27
00:00:56,329 --> 00:00:57,621
(door opens)

28
00:00:57,704 --> 00:01:00,287
Huh? What are you doing in here?

29
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:02,455
Didn't I tell you this
room was ours now

30
00:01:02,538 --> 00:01:04,496
and to stay the hell out of it?

31
00:01:04,996 --> 00:01:06,288
(gasps) Yeah, well...

32
00:01:06,371 --> 00:01:08,788
But you haven't been
using it for weeks, so I...

33
00:01:08,872 --> 00:01:10,788
I just thought it
would be all right!

34
00:01:10,872 --> 00:01:12,456
(slam)

35
00:01:12,539 --> 00:01:14,539
(gasps)

36
00:01:15,706 --> 00:01:17,080
[Itou] So...

37
00:01:17,164 --> 00:01:18,039
So, well, I, um...

38
00:01:18,122 --> 00:01:18,997
(slam)

39
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:21,415
(gasps)

40
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:24,040
Just get your asses out of
here already, you cockroaches!

41
00:01:25,790 --> 00:01:26,832
Come on, Yoshino.

42
00:01:29,208 --> 00:01:30,350
[Itou] Next time we
catch you in here,

43
00:01:30,374 --> 00:01:32,458
we'll send you flying!

44
00:01:32,541 --> 00:01:33,458
(phone beeps)

45
00:01:33,541 --> 00:01:34,458
[Nishimura] Oh yeah, score!

46
00:01:34,541 --> 00:01:36,417
Hey, Junpei, just forget it!

47
00:01:37,417 --> 00:01:39,292
(sighs)

48
00:01:39,375 --> 00:01:41,125
What now?

49
00:01:42,542 --> 00:01:43,662
[Junpei] That belongs to me.

50
00:01:44,375 --> 00:01:46,460
[Itou] So?

51
00:01:46,543 --> 00:01:48,168
(tense music)

52
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:55,294
[Junpei] So...

53
00:01:55,377 --> 00:01:57,419
move your foot.

54
00:02:00,044 --> 00:02:01,795
[Friend] Junpei, just let it go!

55
00:02:02,754 --> 00:02:04,170
No, this belongs to me.

56
00:02:04,253 --> 00:02:06,629
Take your foot off of it.

57
00:02:10,087 --> 00:02:10,296
(whimpering)

58
00:02:10,379 --> 00:02:11,087
(slam)

59
00:02:11,171 --> 00:02:12,087
-Oh damn!
-Oh shit!

60
00:02:12,171 --> 00:02:14,129
(dramatic music)

61
00:02:14,213 --> 00:02:18,547
(breathing heavily)

62
00:02:18,631 --> 00:02:20,881
-Okay!
-I'm outta here!

63
00:02:20,964 --> 00:02:21,964
Okay, okay, we're going!

64
00:02:26,631 --> 00:02:28,715
(pats shoulder)

65
00:02:28,798 --> 00:02:30,381
Close the door.

66
00:02:30,465 --> 00:02:31,590
[Honda] Roger that.

67
00:02:35,256 --> 00:02:37,216
(laughs)

68
00:02:37,299 --> 00:02:40,216
(breathing heavily)

69
00:02:43,633 --> 00:02:48,091
-(pounding)
-(grunting)

70
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:54,092
(Opening Theme Music)

71
00:03:08,677 --> 00:03:12,511
(singing in Japanese)

72
00:04:21,394 --> 00:04:23,353
(water dripping)

73
00:04:29,437 --> 00:04:32,312
[Junpei] I wonder if
the first person to say

74
00:04:32,395 --> 00:04:35,063
"the opposite of
fondness is indifference"

75
00:04:35,146 --> 00:04:36,980
went to hell like
they should have.

76
00:04:38,313 --> 00:04:42,856
Purposely treating people
with malice is never right.

77
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:45,314
A better choice would be
to just leave them alone.

78
00:04:47,606 --> 00:04:50,397
"The opposite of
fondness is hate."

79
00:04:50,481 --> 00:04:53,190
Japanese people love that idea.

80
00:04:53,273 --> 00:04:55,190
They're proud to
take a simple answer

81
00:04:55,273 --> 00:04:56,607
and make it complicated.

82
00:04:58,148 --> 00:05:01,733
[Mahito] The man who coined
that phrase wasn't Japanese.

83
00:05:01,816 --> 00:05:04,441
I'm talking about the
mistaken translation.

84
00:05:04,524 --> 00:05:05,566
[Mahito] Hmm?

85
00:05:05,650 --> 00:05:07,441
[Junpei] The original saying,

86
00:05:07,524 --> 00:05:09,901
as it was first spoken
by some foreigner, was:

87
00:05:09,984 --> 00:05:13,400
"the opposite of love
is indifference," right?

88
00:05:13,484 --> 00:05:17,193
There are lots of
different definitions of love,

89
00:05:17,276 --> 00:05:18,461
so it seems to me
that indifference

90
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:21,443
actually works as
an antonym there.

91
00:05:21,526 --> 00:05:22,568
Yes, true.

92
00:05:24,151 --> 00:05:27,736
But we generally don't use
the word "love" very much.

93
00:05:27,819 --> 00:05:30,110
So I guess that's
why in this country,

94
00:05:30,194 --> 00:05:31,874
it got changed to
"fondness" at some point.

95
00:05:32,611 --> 00:05:34,403
Then that version spread
without any thought

96
00:05:34,487 --> 00:05:37,946
as to whether the
opposing definitions...

97
00:05:38,028 --> 00:05:39,628
of love and indifference
still held true.

98
00:05:41,696 --> 00:05:44,112
Well, everyone
enjoys a little wordplay.

99
00:05:45,029 --> 00:05:46,571
And after all, humans can't live

100
00:05:46,655 --> 00:05:49,238
without making up
excuses for everything.

101
00:05:49,321 --> 00:05:51,697
(eerie music)

102
00:05:55,197 --> 00:05:56,239
What's this?

103
00:05:57,530 --> 00:06:01,114
It was an experiment
to see just how large

104
00:06:01,198 --> 00:06:03,031
I could make a single human.

105
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,490
I made the one you're holding

106
00:06:06,573 --> 00:06:08,614
as an experiment to see
how small I could make them.

107
00:06:10,658 --> 00:06:11,658
Are you saying...

108
00:06:12,699 --> 00:06:14,241
this is...

109
00:06:14,324 --> 00:06:15,367
a human?

110
00:06:16,450 --> 00:06:18,575
[Mahito] Do corpses
bother you, Junpei?

111
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,450
I don't know.

112
00:06:22,617 --> 00:06:25,368
If you had done this to
my mother, well then...

113
00:06:25,451 --> 00:06:28,743
I might lose control
and end up hating you.

114
00:06:30,076 --> 00:06:33,327
But I already know how
repulsive humans can be.

115
00:06:34,744 --> 00:06:36,535
That's why I don't
expect much of anything

116
00:06:36,619 --> 00:06:37,661
from other people.

117
00:06:39,410 --> 00:06:41,651
Nor do I think much of it
when someone I don't know dies.

118
00:06:44,370 --> 00:06:45,411
It's indifference.

119
00:06:45,495 --> 00:06:48,536
That's the virtue one
ought to strive for.

120
00:06:50,454 --> 00:06:53,162
Yet you want revenge...

121
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:54,246
despite that.

122
00:06:55,537 --> 00:06:58,121
Do you see a conflict?
Between the two?

123
00:07:01,121 --> 00:07:04,121
Do you believe human
beings have hearts?

124
00:07:04,205 --> 00:07:06,539
Huh? Why, don't they?

125
00:07:07,581 --> 00:07:09,414
[Mahito] No, they don't.

126
00:07:09,498 --> 00:07:14,206
They have souls, but
souls aren't hearts.

127
00:07:14,289 --> 00:07:15,749
That can't be right!

128
00:07:17,165 --> 00:07:19,332
I'm the only
person in this world

129
00:07:19,415 --> 00:07:21,207
who knows the
soul's composition.

130
00:07:23,124 --> 00:07:26,041
After all, I change the
shape of other creatures

131
00:07:26,124 --> 00:07:27,833
by making contact with them.

132
00:07:27,917 --> 00:07:31,333
All emotions are the result
of the soul's metabolism.

133
00:07:32,584 --> 00:07:34,626
They're far too
mechanical to call hearts.

134
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:39,584
People place too much
value on things they can't see.

135
00:07:39,668 --> 00:07:42,585
I can see them, and
souls are no more special

136
00:07:42,669 --> 00:07:45,085
than physical bodies.

137
00:07:45,168 --> 00:07:47,585
They're just there.
Do you understand?

138
00:07:47,669 --> 00:07:51,086
There's no value or
importance to life.

139
00:07:51,169 --> 00:07:53,086
Life just continues its cycle,

140
00:07:53,169 --> 00:07:54,586
same as the waters of the world.

141
00:07:54,670 --> 00:07:57,545
That's true for both you and me.

142
00:07:58,963 --> 00:08:00,683
Our lives are meaningless
and have no value.

143
00:08:01,796 --> 00:08:04,879
And that's why we can
do anything we want.

144
00:08:04,963 --> 00:08:08,046
We're free to live our
lives however we please.

145
00:08:09,964 --> 00:08:11,088
(gurgling)

146
00:08:11,171 --> 00:08:11,964
Don't let yourself get trapped

147
00:08:12,046 --> 00:08:15,047
by some ideal
concept of indifference.

148
00:08:15,673 --> 00:08:19,881
There's no need for
consistency in living your life.

149
00:08:19,965 --> 00:08:22,507
Just as you eat
when you get hungry,

150
00:08:23,382 --> 00:08:25,298
so it is that if
you hate someone

151
00:08:25,382 --> 00:08:26,674
you can simply kill them.

152
00:08:29,007 --> 00:08:30,590
I'll sanction you fully.

153
00:08:31,883 --> 00:08:33,591
(crumbles)

154
00:08:33,675 --> 00:08:35,716
(emotional music)

155
00:08:42,217 --> 00:08:45,009
(birds whistling)

156
00:08:53,843 --> 00:08:55,718
[Kiyotaka] There he is.

157
00:08:55,802 --> 00:08:56,678
[Yuuji] Huh.
Where's his uniform?

158
00:08:56,761 --> 00:08:59,594
It looks like he hasn't
been attending school

159
00:08:59,678 --> 00:09:00,886
for some time.

160
00:09:01,594 --> 00:09:05,428
Well I guess you could
say the same for me too.

161
00:09:05,512 --> 00:09:06,712
So, hey, how's everyone doing?

162
00:09:06,762 --> 00:09:09,845
(yelling)

163
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:11,720
[Man] Tuna!

164
00:09:12,804 --> 00:09:14,721
From what I hear,
they're doing quite well.

165
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:18,263
So what do we do now?

166
00:09:19,263 --> 00:09:20,638
We're going to use that.

167
00:09:20,721 --> 00:09:21,639
Huh?

168
00:09:21,722 --> 00:09:23,722
Is that a cursed spirit?

169
00:09:23,806 --> 00:09:25,639
It's a fly-head,
alow-level curse

170
00:09:25,722 --> 00:09:27,889
that doesn't even
qualify as a grade Four.

171
00:09:28,639 --> 00:09:31,348
When there are no people around,

172
00:09:31,431 --> 00:09:33,223
we'll release this
curse to attack him.

173
00:09:33,306 --> 00:09:34,515
Huh?

174
00:09:34,598 --> 00:09:36,473
[Kiyotaka] Then one of
four things will happen.

175
00:09:36,556 --> 00:09:39,975
One, if he's a normal person
who can't even see curses,

176
00:09:40,057 --> 00:09:41,349
you will please save him.

177
00:09:42,766 --> 00:09:43,909
Two, if he can
perceive the curse

178
00:09:43,933 --> 00:09:47,392
but has no means to
deal with it, then likewise...

179
00:09:48,976 --> 00:09:50,517
save him please.

180
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:53,517
Afterwards we'll question
him about the theater incident.

181
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:56,768
Three, if he exorcizes
the fly head with jujutsu...

182
00:09:58,518 --> 00:10:00,226
then we immediately
restrain him.

183
00:10:00,309 --> 00:10:00,893
Restrain him how?

184
00:10:00,977 --> 00:10:03,393
By whatever force necessary.

185
00:10:03,476 --> 00:10:04,102
If it's all a misunderstanding,

186
00:10:04,185 --> 00:10:06,394
we'll apologize after the fact.

187
00:10:07,477 --> 00:10:08,852
However...

188
00:10:08,936 --> 00:10:12,478
Four, if Junpei Yoshino
has potential equal

189
00:10:12,561 --> 00:10:13,853
to a grade Two sorcerer...

190
00:10:13,937 --> 00:10:17,103
then we retreat and
report to Nanami.

191
00:10:18,311 --> 00:10:20,020
From what I've
seen, I'm thinking

192
00:10:20,103 --> 00:10:21,854
I can just handle a grade Two.

193
00:10:21,938 --> 00:10:22,729
Not in this case.

194
00:10:22,813 --> 00:10:25,437
[Yuuji] Hm?

195
00:10:25,521 --> 00:10:26,789
[Kiyotaka] Fushiguro
might have mentioned this

196
00:10:26,813 --> 00:10:28,062
to you before.

197
00:10:28,145 --> 00:10:29,814
Typically, cursed
spirits are assigned

198
00:10:29,897 --> 00:10:31,730
to sorcerers of equal grade.

199
00:10:34,355 --> 00:10:35,957
That means a grade Two
sorcerer would be expected

200
00:10:35,981 --> 00:10:38,731
to beat grade
Two cursed spirits.

201
00:10:38,815 --> 00:10:41,064
So a grade Two sorcerer
possesses strength

202
00:10:41,147 --> 00:10:43,189
close to a grade
One cursed spirit.

203
00:10:44,773 --> 00:10:46,565
Why the hell wasn't I ever told

204
00:10:46,649 --> 00:10:48,107
something as important as that?

205
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:51,107
[Kiyotaka] Because
Gojou is irresponsible!

206
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:52,732
(sighs)

207
00:10:52,816 --> 00:10:55,441
We'll get out and
walk from here.

208
00:10:59,358 --> 00:11:00,566
I have to tell you

209
00:11:00,650 --> 00:11:03,109
it feels like I'm the one
doing all the work here.

210
00:11:03,192 --> 00:11:06,234
(suspenseful music)

211
00:11:07,776 --> 00:11:10,818
(dripping)

212
00:11:12,402 --> 00:11:15,443
If you plan to come out,
please hurry up and do so.

213
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:18,860
They may be disfigured
and beyond saving...

214
00:11:20,194 --> 00:11:22,736
but murdering people
still makes me sick.

215
00:11:24,903 --> 00:11:27,778
Ah, what a relief.

216
00:11:28,904 --> 00:11:33,320
I'd be in trouble if
Satoru Gojou were here.

217
00:11:33,404 --> 00:11:35,004
Although the experiment
won't really work

218
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:36,279
if you're too weak.

219
00:11:38,571 --> 00:11:40,947
I hate putting in
overtime if I don't have to.

220
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:44,321
So let's finish this quickly.

221
00:11:44,405 --> 00:11:47,197
(energetic music)

222
00:11:54,490 --> 00:11:55,949
(laughing)

223
00:11:58,907 --> 00:12:01,282
[Satoru] I'll murder you!

224
00:12:02,449 --> 00:12:04,033
[Kento] They're similar.

225
00:12:04,116 --> 00:12:06,741
They both have that same
picture-perfect frivolity

226
00:12:06,825 --> 00:12:10,533
with the sinister
strength behind it.

227
00:12:10,617 --> 00:12:13,034
(splashing)

228
00:12:13,117 --> 00:12:15,450
(grunting)

229
00:12:23,118 --> 00:12:24,035
(laughs)

230
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,451
(grunting)

231
00:12:30,869 --> 00:12:32,077
Huh?

232
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:35,411
I blocked it with
cursed energy, I thought.

233
00:12:35,494 --> 00:12:36,495
Was that your technique?

234
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:39,662
What do you mean?

235
00:12:39,745 --> 00:12:41,203
I hate abstract questions

236
00:12:41,287 --> 00:12:43,704
that leave interpretation
up to others.

237
00:12:43,787 --> 00:12:45,204
That's good.

238
00:12:45,288 --> 00:12:47,162
But you don't hate
chatting evidently.

239
00:12:48,329 --> 00:12:49,579
Not at this time.

240
00:12:50,788 --> 00:12:52,788
This cursed spirit
converses quite well.

241
00:12:52,872 --> 00:12:55,247
Just like the two unregistered

242
00:12:55,330 --> 00:12:57,455
special grades
in Gojou's report.

243
00:12:57,539 --> 00:13:00,706
It would seem highly likely
that there's some connection.

244
00:13:04,164 --> 00:13:05,623
[Mahito] Hey, tell me...

245
00:13:05,707 --> 00:13:09,081
which do you think came
first, the soul or the body?

246
00:13:09,164 --> 00:13:10,249
[Kento] Hm?

247
00:13:10,332 --> 00:13:12,249
Come on. You know.

248
00:13:12,332 --> 00:13:15,457
It's just like the age-old
chicken-or-the-egg question.

249
00:13:15,541 --> 00:13:16,916
Which of them came first?

250
00:13:18,165 --> 00:13:21,458
Do you think the soul
resides in the body,

251
00:13:21,542 --> 00:13:23,625
or do you think it's
the other way around

252
00:13:23,709 --> 00:13:26,125
and the body forms
around the soul?

253
00:13:27,209 --> 00:13:29,418
[Kento] I suppose I
have to listen to this.

254
00:13:30,167 --> 00:13:32,251
The former.

255
00:13:32,334 --> 00:13:33,501
Uh-uh.

256
00:13:33,584 --> 00:13:34,626
It's the second one.

257
00:13:37,003 --> 00:13:40,752
The soul comes first and
so exists before the body.

258
00:13:40,836 --> 00:13:43,294
The shape of the body is
therefore always determined

259
00:13:43,377 --> 00:13:44,378
by the shape of the soul.

260
00:13:46,004 --> 00:13:47,086
I'm not healing now.

261
00:13:47,169 --> 00:13:50,586
I'm just maintaining the
shape of my own soul.

262
00:13:53,838 --> 00:13:55,038
You understand now, don't you?

263
00:13:55,087 --> 00:13:58,963
My technique is to make
contact with the soul,

264
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,797
and then alter its shape.

265
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:02,880
Idle Transfiguration!

266
00:14:05,630 --> 00:14:06,880
(gasps)

267
00:14:06,964 --> 00:14:09,965
I keep a human stockpile.

268
00:14:10,048 --> 00:14:11,589
It's been difficult though.

269
00:14:13,256 --> 00:14:16,589
Normal people die soon
after their shape is transfigured.

270
00:14:17,757 --> 00:14:20,173
I wonder if jujutsu
sorcerers last longer.

271
00:14:22,799 --> 00:14:27,842
It's 5:30 now, and I began
my day at 10:00 this morning,

272
00:14:27,925 --> 00:14:29,466
so I'm quitting at 6:00,

273
00:14:29,550 --> 00:14:31,550
regardless of
what that requires.

274
00:14:39,092 --> 00:14:40,092
[Sotomura] Yoshino!

275
00:14:40,175 --> 00:14:41,175
Huh?

276
00:14:41,217 --> 00:14:42,217
Where were ya today?

277
00:14:43,011 --> 00:14:44,552
(groans)

278
00:14:44,635 --> 00:14:47,760
Missed you at school. You
shouldn't be skipping class.

279
00:14:47,844 --> 00:14:49,844
Of course, sir. I know that.

280
00:14:51,011 --> 00:14:54,344
Anyway, did you hear
about those theater murders?

281
00:14:54,428 --> 00:14:55,303
It's all over the news.

282
00:14:55,386 --> 00:14:59,094
Sayama, Nishimura
and Honda are all dead!

283
00:14:59,177 --> 00:15:00,220
(gasps)

284
00:15:00,304 --> 00:15:02,554
(cackling)

285
00:15:02,637 --> 00:15:05,512
You were friends with all three
of those boys, weren't you?

286
00:15:06,262 --> 00:15:07,387
They spent time with you

287
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:09,055
when you had no
other friends, right?

288
00:15:09,138 --> 00:15:09,930
But you didn't go
to their funerals.

289
00:15:10,014 --> 00:15:12,014
[Junpei] Friends?

290
00:15:12,096 --> 00:15:13,722
Me...

291
00:15:13,805 --> 00:15:14,930
and them?

292
00:15:15,014 --> 00:15:17,015
He must be insane.

293
00:15:19,056 --> 00:15:20,639
You teachers...

294
00:15:20,723 --> 00:15:22,264
You graduate from school,

295
00:15:22,347 --> 00:15:25,390
and then you go to work
in those same schools.

296
00:15:25,473 --> 00:15:28,140
So you never actually
experience the real world, do you?

297
00:15:31,057 --> 00:15:32,283
That's how we end up
with overgrown children

298
00:15:32,307 --> 00:15:34,766
like you in charge, isn't it?

299
00:15:35,308 --> 00:15:37,975
Here! Say "Ah"!

300
00:15:38,058 --> 00:15:38,975
(cackles)

301
00:15:39,058 --> 00:15:41,266
[Junpei] It's true of
every last one of them!

302
00:15:41,349 --> 00:15:42,350
Smile! Say cheese!

303
00:15:44,350 --> 00:15:46,392
[Mahito] You can
simply kill them.

304
00:15:46,475 --> 00:15:47,225
I'll sanction you fully.

305
00:15:47,309 --> 00:15:50,059
(gasps)

306
00:15:51,518 --> 00:15:53,643
What in the world are you
mumbling about, Junpei?

307
00:15:53,727 --> 00:15:55,060
Did self-isolation
fry your brain?

308
00:15:55,143 --> 00:15:58,601
(laughs)

309
00:15:58,685 --> 00:15:59,686
(gasps)

310
00:15:59,728 --> 00:16:02,519
(dramatic music)

311
00:16:03,894 --> 00:16:05,269
[Yuuji] Stop!

312
00:16:05,352 --> 00:16:06,269
(yelling)

313
00:16:06,352 --> 00:16:08,437
[Junpei] What the hell is that?

314
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,437
Whoa!

315
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:10,270
This guy...

316
00:16:10,353 --> 00:16:12,520
can see the curse!

317
00:16:14,270 --> 00:16:15,186
(shouts)

318
00:16:15,270 --> 00:16:17,022
(grunts)

319
00:16:17,104 --> 00:16:20,022
Ow! That freakin' hurt!

320
00:16:21,521 --> 00:16:22,104
Look around.

321
00:16:22,187 --> 00:16:24,647
Here we go, Itadori!

322
00:16:24,731 --> 00:16:26,480
Time out! There's someone there!

323
00:16:26,564 --> 00:16:27,480
Huh?

324
00:16:27,564 --> 00:16:28,605
Oh, no!

325
00:16:29,105 --> 00:16:32,105
That was close!

326
00:16:32,188 --> 00:16:34,523
What's this? Where
did you come from?

327
00:16:35,356 --> 00:16:38,106
Hey, I've got a few things
I'd like to ask you about.

328
00:16:38,189 --> 00:16:39,648
Got a sec?

329
00:16:39,732 --> 00:16:41,357
Uh, I was...

330
00:16:41,441 --> 00:16:42,149
[Yuuji] Come with me.

331
00:16:42,232 --> 00:16:43,149
[Junpei] That button!

332
00:16:43,232 --> 00:16:44,149
[Sotomura] Hold on,

333
00:16:44,232 --> 00:16:46,733
Junpei and I were
having a conversation!

334
00:16:46,816 --> 00:16:48,066
Don't be rude!

335
00:16:48,149 --> 00:16:51,900
Ah, well, this concerns
something rather important.

336
00:16:51,984 --> 00:16:52,608
What's important?

337
00:16:52,692 --> 00:16:55,026
You're just another stupid kid!

338
00:16:55,108 --> 00:16:56,358
And what kind of uniform is-

339
00:16:56,442 --> 00:16:57,358
(shouts)

340
00:16:57,442 --> 00:16:58,901
(yells) Hey!

341
00:16:58,985 --> 00:16:59,901
(gasps)

342
00:16:59,985 --> 00:17:01,027
(yells)

343
00:17:01,109 --> 00:17:03,359
What the hell do you
think you're doing, you brat?

344
00:17:03,443 --> 00:17:04,443
Let go of my pants!

345
00:17:06,068 --> 00:17:06,986
No, don't!

346
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:09,569
Stop! Get back here with those!

347
00:17:12,610 --> 00:17:14,694
Come back! Wait!

348
00:17:14,777 --> 00:17:17,278
(energetic music)

349
00:17:17,361 --> 00:17:19,320
What was that all about?

350
00:17:19,403 --> 00:17:20,320
Huh?

351
00:17:20,403 --> 00:17:22,278
Okay, let's talk!

352
00:17:22,361 --> 00:17:23,194
[Junpei] You went
around the block already?

353
00:17:23,278 --> 00:17:25,321
That was fast!

354
00:17:25,404 --> 00:17:26,571
Yeah.

355
00:17:26,654 --> 00:17:28,738
You didn't have to
go to all that trouble.

356
00:17:28,821 --> 00:17:30,279
You could have just
dragged me away.

357
00:17:30,362 --> 00:17:32,238
[Yuuji] Yeah, sure, I
guess I could have.

358
00:17:32,322 --> 00:17:35,822
But you hate that
guy, don't you?

359
00:17:35,905 --> 00:17:36,780
Huh?

360
00:17:36,864 --> 00:17:38,280
How did you...

361
00:17:38,363 --> 00:17:40,196
Oh, just a hunch.

362
00:17:41,114 --> 00:17:42,281
Or am I wrong?

363
00:17:42,364 --> 00:17:44,197
[Junpei] No, you're not wrong.

364
00:17:44,281 --> 00:17:45,740
You don't want someone you hate

365
00:17:45,823 --> 00:17:48,406
hanging around outside
your house now do you?

366
00:17:48,489 --> 00:17:50,907
So how 'bout we take a walk?

367
00:17:54,282 --> 00:17:56,157
Sure.

368
00:17:58,325 --> 00:18:01,908
(intense music)

369
00:18:07,659 --> 00:18:08,993
(grunts)

370
00:18:09,076 --> 00:18:10,326
Your speed's impressive.

371
00:18:13,409 --> 00:18:15,535
(shouts)

372
00:18:24,037 --> 00:18:25,161
This is so fun!

373
00:18:25,244 --> 00:18:28,453
[Kento] So the person's
original mass is irrelevant

374
00:18:28,536 --> 00:18:30,453
when it comes to
changing their shape.

375
00:18:32,871 --> 00:18:35,746
Either way, it's a bad
match-up for my technique.

376
00:18:39,663 --> 00:18:41,663
Please, help me!

377
00:18:44,371 --> 00:18:46,371
There's nothing you can do

378
00:18:46,455 --> 00:18:48,622
to save someone
once they're reshaped.

379
00:18:48,706 --> 00:18:51,122
If they start to attack,
you must kill them.

380
00:18:51,205 --> 00:18:52,998
It's better for the
victims that way.

381
00:18:56,081 --> 00:18:58,874
Ah, yeah, sorry about that.

382
00:18:58,957 --> 00:19:00,332
I had to really
practice a lot...

383
00:19:00,415 --> 00:19:03,206
so they wouldn't die right
away when I changed their size.

384
00:19:03,290 --> 00:19:04,206
And yet...

385
00:19:04,290 --> 00:19:06,291
do they know?

386
00:19:06,374 --> 00:19:09,000
I don't know precisely
how aware they are.

387
00:19:09,083 --> 00:19:12,499
And as a result sometimes
their souls sweat like that one.

388
00:19:12,583 --> 00:19:13,959
Don't let that worry you.

389
00:19:15,709 --> 00:19:17,375
[Kento] I'm not
worried about it.

390
00:19:20,917 --> 00:19:25,044
It's my policy not to bring
personal feelings into my work.

391
00:19:25,126 --> 00:19:25,543
(laughing)

392
00:19:25,626 --> 00:19:27,460
You suck at lying!

393
00:19:27,543 --> 00:19:30,168
Your whole soul is trembling!

394
00:19:30,251 --> 00:19:31,252
So you're...

395
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,252
what grade?

396
00:19:32,336 --> 00:19:33,502
[Kento] Grade One.

397
00:19:33,586 --> 00:19:36,711
No wonder you're strong.

398
00:19:36,794 --> 00:19:39,920
You'll make the
perfect test subject.

399
00:19:40,004 --> 00:19:41,587
Luck's really on my side.

400
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:44,545
I'm grateful.

401
00:19:45,795 --> 00:19:48,171
(groaning)

402
00:19:50,421 --> 00:19:53,713
Are you surprised my
speed suddenly increased?

403
00:19:53,796 --> 00:19:56,964
The fact is I can alter the
shape of my own soul, too.

404
00:19:57,464 --> 00:19:59,505
Jujutsu sorcerers can
protect their bodies

405
00:19:59,589 --> 00:20:03,380
with cursed energy, but they
aren't protecting their souls.

406
00:20:03,464 --> 00:20:07,173
For starters, you have to
be aware of your own soul.

407
00:20:07,256 --> 00:20:09,923
It's not possible to
protect it if you're not.

408
00:20:10,007 --> 00:20:12,548
But it looks to me like you
subconsciously covered your soul

409
00:20:12,632 --> 00:20:15,091
somewhat with cursed energy.

410
00:20:15,174 --> 00:20:18,215
If you hadn't done that you'd
already be under my control.

411
00:20:19,174 --> 00:20:20,358
Though, once I touch
you a few more times

412
00:20:20,382 --> 00:20:23,467
you will cease to
be human anymore!

413
00:20:25,009 --> 00:20:27,051
(grunts)

414
00:20:33,217 --> 00:20:34,217
I'm not letting you go!

415
00:20:48,553 --> 00:20:51,762
Was that it, grade One sorcerer?

416
00:20:51,845 --> 00:20:53,428
You did well running around,

417
00:20:53,511 --> 00:20:55,637
but you're at your
limit now, aren't you?

418
00:20:56,429 --> 00:20:59,262
(ticking)

419
00:20:59,346 --> 00:21:01,471
(sighs)

420
00:21:01,554 --> 00:21:03,889
Unfortunately...

421
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:06,930
[Mahito] What?

422
00:21:08,056 --> 00:21:09,930
His cursed energy's increasing?

423
00:21:10,722 --> 00:21:12,431
Thanks to you...

424
00:21:12,514 --> 00:21:14,723
I'm going to have
to go into overtime.

425
00:21:16,057 --> 00:21:19,098
(Closing Theme Music)

426
00:21:22,891 --> 00:21:26,891
(singing in Japanese)

427
00:22:45,817 --> 00:22:47,525
[Group] Juju Stroll!

428
00:22:47,609 --> 00:22:48,525
(light percussive music)

429
00:22:48,609 --> 00:22:50,233
Fushiguro!

430
00:22:50,317 --> 00:22:52,068
Seen my uniform jacket?

431
00:22:52,150 --> 00:22:52,609
I haven't.

432
00:22:52,692 --> 00:22:54,902
Whoa, that's so weird!

433
00:22:54,985 --> 00:22:55,985
I left it right here.

434
00:22:56,818 --> 00:22:57,735
Oh!

435
00:22:57,818 --> 00:22:58,735
Hey Panda?

436
00:22:58,818 --> 00:23:01,193
Have you seen my
jacket anywhere?

437
00:23:01,276 --> 00:23:02,402
Hm...

438
00:23:02,486 --> 00:23:03,778
No, sorry...

439
00:23:06,028 --> 00:23:07,402
Okay...

440
00:23:07,486 --> 00:23:09,944
I wonder where it
could have gone.

441
00:23:10,028 --> 00:23:13,487
-(shouts)
-(grunts)

442
00:23:13,570 --> 00:23:17,653
Hey! My skirt's not here
either, you clothing klepto!

443
00:23:17,737 --> 00:23:19,237
Now you've gone too far!

444
00:23:21,988 --> 00:23:22,738
[Toge] Mustard leaf!

445
00:23:22,821 --> 00:23:25,821
(snarling)

446
00:23:27,030 --> 00:23:28,405
[Nobara] You're both trash!

447
00:23:28,489 --> 00:23:29,947
Bonito flakes!

448
00:23:30,031 --> 00:23:31,947
[Megumi] What am I looking at?

449
00:23:32,031 --> 00:23:32,947
Huh?

450
00:23:33,031 --> 00:23:34,197
What the?

451
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:35,823
This is Maki's skirt!

452
00:23:38,615 --> 00:23:39,990
Hey, check me out!

453
00:23:40,074 --> 00:23:42,365
I'm Nobara Kuuugisaki!

454
00:23:42,448 --> 00:23:45,449
(laughing)

455
00:23:45,532 --> 00:23:48,240
(dramatic music)

